@page "/kanban/showhide-columns"

@using Syncfusion.Blazor.KanbanDemo
@using Syncfusion.Blazor.Buttons
@using Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban
@*Hidden:Lines*@
@inherits SampleBaseComponent;
@*End:Hidden*@

<ActionDescription>
<p>
    This sample demonstrates how to change column visibility dynamically in the <a class="e-kanban-showhidecolumns-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the explore Syncfusion Blazor Kanban component"
                                                                                                                                  href="https://www.syncfusion.com/gantt-sdk/blazor-kanban-board"
                                                                                                                                  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blazor Kanban</a> component by visualizing a Menu Development. Use the property panel checkboxes to show or hide specific columns across To Do, In Progress, Testing, and Close stages.
</p>
<p>
    Toggle column visibility using the <a class="e-kanban-showhidecolumns-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of Visible property in Kanban"
                                                                                                                                  href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.KanbanColumn.html#Syncfusion_Blazor_Kanban_KanbanColumn_Visible"
                                                                                                                                  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visible</a> property on each KanbanColumn.
</p>
<p>
    Additional essential interactions that enhance analysis and control are also featured:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the columns in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/columns"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Columns</a>: Group cards by workflow stage such as To Do, In Progress, Testing, and Close.
    </li>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the drag and drop in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/drag-and-drop"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Drag and Drop</a>: Move cards between the visible columns to update their workflow status.
    </li>
</ul>
<p>
    Key interactive features demonstrated in this sample include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Show or Hide</b>: Use the property panel checkboxes to toggle the visibility of each column.</li>
    <li><b>Live Layout</b>: The board re-renders as columns are shown or hidden, keeping the visible columns properly sized.</li>
    <li><b>Card Persistence</b>: Cards in hidden columns remain in the data source and reappear when the column is shown again.</li>
    <li><b>Multi-Column Toggle</b>: Multiple columns can be shown or hidden at the same time using the property panel.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    The <b>Property Panel</b> offers quick toggles for managing the visible columns:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Column Checkbox</b>: Each column has a dedicated checkbox to show or hide it on the board.</li>
    <li><b>Layout Adjust</b>: The board automatically adjusts the layout as columns are shown or hidden.</li>
    <li><b>Persistence</b>: The visibility state is preserved in the component data, so the chosen layout is retained.</li>
</ul>
<p>
Looking for the full Blazor Kanban component overview, features, pricing, and documentation? Visit the <a class="e-kanban-showhidecolumns-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the explore Syncfusion Blazor Kanban component" href="https://www.syncfusion.com/gantt-sdk/blazor-kanban-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blazor Kanban</a> page.</p>
</ActionDescription>


<div class="col-lg-9 control-section">
    <SfKanban KeyField="Status" DataSource="@CardData" Height="500px">
        <KanbanColumns>
            @foreach (ColumnModel item in ColumnData)
            {
                <KanbanColumn HeaderText="@item.HeaderText" KeyField="@item.KeyField" Visible="@item.Visible"/>
            }
        </KanbanColumns>
        <KanbanCardSettings HeaderField="Id" ContentField="Summary">
    <Template>
        @{
            KanbanDataModel card = (KanbanDataModel)context;
            <div class="min-card" style="--color: @card.Color;">
                <div class="mc-strip"></div>
                <div class="mc-content">
                    <div class="mc-head">
                        <span class="mc-type">@card.Type</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="mc-title">@card.Title</h3>
                    <p class="mc-desc">@card.Summary</p>
                    <div class="mc-footer">
                        <span class="mc-priority" data-p="@card.Priority">@card.Priority</span>
                        <span class="mc-id">@card.Id</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        }
    </Template>
</KanbanCardSettings>
    </SfKanban>
</div>
<PropertyPanel ControlSecClass="col-lg-9">
    <table class="property-panel-table" title="Show/Hide Columns">
        <tbody>
            @foreach (ColumnModel item in ColumnData)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 100%">
                        <SfCheckBox TChecked="bool" @bind-Checked="@item.Visible" Label="@item.HeaderText" ValueChange="@((args) => item.Visible = args.Checked)"/>
                    </td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</PropertyPanel>

<style>
    .sf-property-panel-section table {
        width: 100%;
    }

    .sf-property-panel-section table tr {
        height: 50px;
    }

    .sf-property-panel-section table td {
        padding-left: 10px;
        width: 50%;
    }

    .sf-property-section .e-icons.e-settings,
    .sf-property-panel-header {
        height: 0;
    }
        .min-card { display: flex; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; 
                box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.08); 
                transition: all .3s cubic-bezier(.25,.46,.45,.94); border: 1px solid #f0f0f0; }
    .min-card:hover { box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.12); transform: translateY(-3px); 
                      border-color: var(--color); }
    .mc-strip { width: 5px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,.1) 100%); flex-shrink: 0; }
    .mc-content { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; min-width: 0; }
    .mc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; line-height: normal; padding: 5px;  }
    .mc-type { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; background: rgba(0,0,0,.05); 
               padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; border-left: 3px solid var(--color); text-transform: uppercase; }
    .mc-avatar { width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color); 
                 color: #fff; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; 
                 font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.15); 
                 transition: transform .2s; }
    .min-card:hover .mc-avatar { transform: scale(1.12); }
    .mc-title { padding-left: 5px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;  margin: 0; line-height: 1.3; }
    .mc-desc { padding: 5px; font-size: 11px; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4; }
    .mc-footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 10px; 
                 padding: 8px; border-top: 1px dashed #e5e5e5; font-weight: 600; line-height: normal; }
    .mc-priority { padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #f5f5f5; }
    .mc-priority[data-p="High"] { background: #fce4e4; color: var(--color-sf-warning-bg-color); }
    .mc-priority[data-p="Low"] { background: #e8f5e9; color: var(--color-sf-success-dark); }
    .mc-priority[data-p="Normal"] { background: #e3f2fd; color: var(--color-sf-primary-label-color);}
